says       SO_SNDTIMEO set to 1.5 seconds on an AF_UNIX stream socket reads
           back as a struct timeval no smaller than that (it may have been
           rounded up); a set that fails with ENOPROTOOPT or EINVAL leaves
           the test not in use.
test       t/010-sndtimeo.c

assertion  XSH.setsockopt.011
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.10.16
class      disputed
since      2001
says       With SO_RCVTIMEO set to 200 ms, a blocking recv() on an empty
           stream socket fails with EAGAIN or EWOULDBLOCK after waiting at
           least that long (the clock's resolution allowed for).
note       disputed (Q-211): the timeout is called the limit on how long to
           wait and nothing says a receive may not give up a little before
           it; the test takes the lower bound, and a FAIL (an early return)
           is logged as INSPECT.
test       t/011-rcvtimeo-effect.c

assertion  XSH.setsockopt.012
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.10.16
class      required
since      2001
says       With SO_RCVTIMEO set to 20 s, a blocking recv() on a stream
           socket that receives a byte 200 ms later returns the byte, not a
           timeout failure.
test       t/012-rcvtimeo-data.c

assertion  XSH.setsockopt.013
anchor     functions/setsockopt.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.10.16
anchor     functions/send.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With SO_SNDTIMEO set to 200 ms, a blocking send() on a stream
           socket whose send space is full fails with EAGAIN or EWOULDBLOCK
           after waiting at least that long (the clock's resolution allowed
           for).
test       t/013-sndtimeo-effect.c

assertion  XSH.setsockopt.014
anchor     functions/setsockopt.html#ERRORS/EDOM
class      required
since      2001
says       setsockopt() of SO_RCVTIMEO with the largest possible tv_sec
           either succeeds or fails with EDOM (the value too big for the
           socket's timeout field); ENOPROTOOPT leaves the test not in use.
note       The page says the error is for values too big for the field, so
           a system whose field holds the value succeeds; any other failure
           is wrong.
test       t/014-timeout-edom.c

assertion  XSH.setsockopt.015
anchor     functions/setsockopt.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       setsockopt() with a descriptor that is not open fails with EBADF
           (-1, and a closed descriptor).
test       t/015-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.setsockopt.016
anchor     functions/setsockopt.html#ERRORS/ENOTSOCK
class      required
since      2001
says       setsockopt() on a descriptor that is not a socket (a pipe end, a
           regular file) fails with ENOTSOCK.
